################################################################################
# This .gitignore file was automatically created by Microsoft(R) Visual Studio.
################################################################################

/bin/Debug/net9.0
/bin/Release/net9.0/wwwroot/_framework
/bin/Release/net9.0
/obj
/.vs/oxyniti
/.vs/Oxyniti
/.vs
# Blue Sharc: .sharc/ is a mix of machine-local runtime caches (cracked
# substrate .rac files, peer/provider configs with this machine's absolute
# install path, session logs) and derived files (state.json/tree.json/
# governance.json, 100% rebuilt from evolution/manifest.toml by tree.build on
# every pull/merge/checkout via the post-merge/post-checkout hook). None of
# that is shareable or should ever be hand-edited or committed -- only the
# Goal/Epic/Feature/Story source of truth is.
.sharc/*
!.sharc/evolution
.sharc/evolution/*
# The event log IS the shared artifact: authoring appends here and every
# developer needs it. The blanket .sharc/evolution/* rule above would swallow
# it, leaving everyone with a PRIVATE backlog, so re-include it explicitly.
!.sharc/evolution/events.jsonl
# ...and the SHARD DIRECTORY. The log is one file per (actor, branch) so two
# branches never write the same file -- that, not a merge driver, is what makes
# concurrent PRs conflict-free. A negation cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the directory is re-included first.
!.sharc/evolution/events/
!.sharc/evolution/events/*.jsonl
# LEGACY: manifest.toml was the old committed intent store (retired 2026-08-03).
# Two developers patching one TOML file conflicted on every concurrent edit.
# Nothing reads it now; kept locally as history, no longer tracked.
.sharc/evolution/manifest.toml
